  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e992638c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This tutorial and the assets can be downloaded as part of the [Wallaroo Tutorials repository](https://github.com/WallarooLabs/Wallaroo_Tutorials/blob/wallaroo2026.1_tutorials/wallaroo-llms/rag-llms/vector-database-embedding-with-ml-orchestrations).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Llama 8B in SGLang Framework with ROCm AI Acceleration Example\n",
    "\n",
    "The following example demonstrates deploying a LLM using the Wallaroo SGLang framework with ROCm AI Acceleration enabled.\n",
    "\n",
    "The tutorial demonstrates:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Retrieving a LLM in the [Wallaroo SGLang framework](http://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-deployment/wallaroo-deployment-model-packaging/wallaroo-deployment-model-llm/llm-upload-procedure/vllm-upload-sglang/) configured with ROCm acceleration.\n",
    "* Setting [Wallaroo continuous batching](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-inference/wallaroo-inference-high-performance-serving/high-performance-serving-llm/wallaroo-llm-optimizations-continuous-batching/) options and [OpenAI compatibility options](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-inference/wallaroo-inference-portability/wallaroo-inference-portability-applications/wallaroo-llm-optimizations-openai-compatibility/).\n",
    "* Deploying the LLM with deployment configuration options\n",
    "* Performing a sample inference.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "For access to these sample models and for a demonstration of how to use a LLM Validation Listener.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Contact your Wallaroo Support Representative **OR**\n",
    "* [Schedule Your Wallaroo.AI Demo Today](https://wallaroo.ai/request-a-demo/).\n",
    "\n",
    "## References\n",
    "\n",
    "* [How to Upload and Deploy SGLang Framework Models](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-deployment/wallaroo-deployment-model-packaging/wallaroo-deployment-model-llm/llm-upload-procedure/vllm-upload-sglang/)\n",
    "* [Continuous Batching for LLMs](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-inference/wallaroo-inference-high-performance-serving/high-performance-serving-llm/wallaroo-llm-optimizations-continuous-batching/)\n",
    "* [Deploy LLMs with OpenAI Compatibility](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-inference/wallaroo-inference-portability/wallaroo-inference-portability-applications/wallaroo-llm-optimizations-openai-compatibility/)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e59d4cef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tutorial Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "### Import Python Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "The first step is to import the libraries used for this tutorial, primarily the [Wallaroo SDK](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-developer-guides/wallaroo-sdk-guides/)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "7501159b-1be6-44ab-a972-2cbb0e4f380c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pyarrow as pa\n",
    "import wallaroo\n",
    "\n",
    "from wallaroo.framework import Framework\n",
    "from wallaroo.engine_config import Acceleration\n",
    "from wallaroo.openai_config import OpenaiConfig\n",
    "from wallaroo.continuous_batching_config import ContinuousBatchingConfig\n",
    "from wallaroo.framework import SGLangConfig, VLLMConfig"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "313c784c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Connect to the Wallaroo Instance\n",
    "\n",
    "This step sets a connection to Wallaroo through the Wallaroo client.  The Python library is included in the Wallaroo install and available through the Jupyter Hub interface provided with your Wallaroo environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is accomplished using the `wallaroo.Client()` command, which provides a URL to grant the SDK permission to your specific Wallaroo environment.  When displayed, enter the URL into a browser and confirm permissions.  Store the connection into a variable that can be referenced later.\n",
    "\n",
    "If logging into the Wallaroo instance through the internal JupyterHub service, use `wl = wallaroo.Client()`.  For more information on Wallaroo Client settings, see the [Client Connection guide](https://docs.wallaroo.ai/wallaroo-developer-guides/wallaroo-sdk-guides/wallaroo-sdk-essentials-guide/wallaroo-sdk-essentials-client/)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0aa5ff1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wl = wallaroo.Client()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44ce4669",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
